# What is deliberately kept out of the repository, and why.
#
# Everything else in this directory is tracked: sources, tests, build script,
# docs (including the requirements document), and the profile manifests. A clone
# plus `npm install` is enough to build and install the plugin.

# ── Installed dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `lib/index.js` (host bundle) and `lib/client.js` (browser bundle) are produced
# by `npm run build`. They are derived artifacts, so they are not committed.
#
# The caveat, because it bites: a
#   dsh plugin --profile web add link:<this directory>
# install loads `lib/` straight out of this directory, so the build must have run
# at least once first. `npm install` covers it — the `prepare` script builds —
# and `npm run build` does it explicitly. A checkout that was never built fails
# loudly at `dsh web` startup ("missing bundle") rather than silently.
lib/

# TypeScript incremental build state, should a composite build ever be enabled.
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Machine-local tooling state ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The session sandbox cannot write to `~/.npm`, so npm's cache is redirected in
# here (see `.npmrc`). Large, machine-local, and never portable.
.tooling/

# ── Editor project state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# JetBrains' `.idea/` — module settings, inspection profiles, open-file history.
# It belongs to whoever has the project open rather than to the project, and it
# rewrites itself while the repository is only being read.
.idea/

# ── Scratch DSH homes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A throwaway `$DSH_HOME` for booting an isolated instance to verify the plugin
# without disturbing a running one. It accumulates credentials, session logs, and
# plugin state, so it must never be committed.
.verify/

# ── Cross-project scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Notes written while working on someone else's repository: issue drafts, an
# implementation checklist, a community-channel crib sheet. They belong to a
# different project, so they are not this repository's history — they stay on
# disk and out of the tree.
contrib/

# ── Sandbox clone of a real remote ───────────────────────────────────────────
# `test/dsh-git-plugin-sandbox` is a clone of a throwaway GitHub repository,
# used to drive the panel against a real HTTPS remote. It is another
# repository's history, and a nested work tree would otherwise appear here as an
# untracked directory.
#
# It is also named in `tsconfig.json`'s `exclude`, because it is another
# repository: it has to be free to sit in whatever state its own experiments
# leave it — including a conflicted merge, whose markers are not TypeScript —
# without turning this repository's `npm run check` red.
test/dsh-git-plugin-sandbox/
